        "sha256": "97171e79bf890c5965580a1d15b6e7845344aab91256586028e4c38f61f6a4a0",
        "signing_date": "1943-09-23",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_9379.txt",
        "text_sha256": "eca0b06595d4c4a9bc4e6a0d408adab95144fb225561da8c7b10fe0ebb2d6ecc",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1943-09-28/pdf/FR-1943-09-28.pdf"
      },
      "text": "1. There is hereby established a Spe­\ncial Emergency Board of three members \nto be selected by me from the National \nRailway Labor panel who shall report \nto me what, if any, wage adustments \nfor employees of the Pacific Electric \nRailway Company of Los Angeles, Cali­\nfornia, should be made, within the limi­\ntations of the Act of October 2, 1942 and \nthe Executive Orders and Directives is­\nsued thereunder. The Board’s report \nshall be based upon the proceedings be­\nfore the Emergency Board that reported \nto me May 21, 1943 on this dispute, the \nrelevant, factual material in the Madris \nReport filed with the National Railway \nLabor panel September 10,1943 and such \nfurther relevant evidence as the Special \nEmergency Board shall determine to re­\nceive."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2380,
      "char_start": 2113,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:9379#2",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "2.",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "scope_id": "EO:9379#2",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "8 FR 13081, PDF pages 1-1",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "97171e79bf890c5965580a1d15b6e7845344aab91256586028e4c38f61f6a4a0",
        "signing_date": "1943-09-23",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_9379.txt",
        "text_sha256": "eca0b06595d4c4a9bc4e6a0d408adab95144fb225561da8c7b10fe0ebb2d6ecc",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1943-09-28/pdf/FR-1943-09-28.pdf"
      },
      "text": "2. The Special Emergency Board shall \nreport to the President on or before Oc­\ntober 15, 1943. Copies of the report \nshall be filed at the same time with the \nEconomic Stabilization Director, the Na­\ntional War Labor Board, and the Com­\nmissioner of Internal Revenue."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 3028,
      "char_start": 2381,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:9379#3",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "3.",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "scope_id": "EO:9379#3",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "8 FR 13081, PDF pages 1-1",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "97171e79bf890c5965580a1d15b6e7845344aab91256586028e4c38f61f6a4a0",
        "signing_date": "1943-09-23",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_9379.txt",
        "text_sha256": "eca0b06595d4c4a9bc4e6a0d408adab95144fb225561da8c7b10fe0ebb2d6ecc",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1943-09-28/pdf/FR-1943-09-28.pdf"
      },
      "text": "3. The Economic Stabilization Director \nshall on behalf of himself or other De­\npartments and Agencies concerned re­\nport to the President the effect of the \nrecommendations on the general stabili­\nzation program. The report of the Eco­\nnomic Stabilization Director shall be \nmade within ten days after the date on \nwhich the Special Emergency Board’s\nreport has been filed. At the time of \nthe Director’s report the recommenda­\ntions of the Special Emergency Board \nin regard to proposed changes affecting \nwages and salary payments shall become \neffective, unless and except to the extent \nthe Economic Stabilization Director \notherwise directs."
    }
  ],
